{"title":"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a parallelogram and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32fc49a92816e8efd9197984c45e8f049a9b6bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{AA^\\prime}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"23\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a703dd7e11cb786f438e6e07744c8bf071b33f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{BB^\\prime}$\" width=\"33\" height=\"23\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2be055ba311a1f031bd254df1a0df4b4fdf6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{CC^\\prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"22\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/0/1f0edae3c2c3f425a43f50b00163e5a4ac5d7e79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{DD^\\prime}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"23\" /> be parallel rays in space on the same side of the plane determined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c639374b8efaec3bc3b1fd59d11de533ddca59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA^{\\prime} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296ab14715afe33a101133f6fac45b9c7843be55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB^{\\prime}= 8$\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/676b61a7546149825753d24de2570897f8857b2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC^\\prime = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89ed394ce88b3417681664a01ecf15127921aa20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DD^\\prime = 22$\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are the midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48c216c2bfb047dc9e5fa2ebb8aef6d65cf3702e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^{\\prime} C^{\\prime}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/097f3e2025ce1c14ba6e86f772c2a68d21ada489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B^{\\prime}D^{\\prime}$\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/2927edfaa2a0512b9f5d4d8e4c34fe3e2f697bf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN =$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3ad07ba45d9a4dcd46fbd971320abb2585f7ce0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a unit square with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f61d0f354191943c4ade0a76811e2ed093f7581.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(0,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac1343a7d5ffb757988b9eda707fdd985f594892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(0,1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/7200f39c53ccf47c2c7735f516d34d4920216727.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(1,1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107ce27eab331caa49ff70fddc5f461021efb62d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(1,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />.  Assume that the rays go in the +z direction.  In this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa71e79fac4f66826352215134f77d2ab58d5c1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^\\prime(0,0,10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/4536e344760bc06e82ea8b0e00e5e7a2b2ecc509.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B^\\prime(0,1,8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/2/1123133604f87e19c11ae5946efdefc053c6eb60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C^\\prime(1,1,18)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40a9d9d1c185a2420857f8048be57e3ab90db0a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D^\\prime(1,0,22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />.  Finding the midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502246c7435aea2819dd04b8d3eeaf49eda7f4c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^\\prime C^\\prime$\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1dbaa73f18aca9c7439cae08b816bcad3d6662b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B^\\prime D^\\prime$\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f24c60790dd2ac0e24e6bef324a6a3981712c58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}, 14)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc654215d98edd45b126b37f4296d7815a769560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N(\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}, 15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"37\" />.  The distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e852cad244e16079fd12c852235cddb089130d87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 - 14 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.    \n</p><p><br />\nWhile this solution is not a proof, the problem asks for a value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> that is supposed to be an invariant.  Additional assumptions that are consistient with the problem's premise should not change the answer.  The assumptions made in this solution are that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a square, and that all rays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/f/8bf14369ac912cc127285e0214a46e58ab43e06b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XX^\\prime$\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> are perpendicular to the plane of the square.  These assumptions are consistient with all facts of the problem.  Additionally, the assumptions allow for a quick solution to the problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME\" title=\"1997 AHSME\">1997 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1997 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1997\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017014532\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 243/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6190/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.282      1 -total\n 60.18%    7.993      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 38.24%    5.079      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10011:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017014532 and revision id 271814. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}